│ To address the issue of a 1-element tuple being rendered           │
│ incorrectly in Sphinx, we need to modify the logic that handles    │
│ tuple rendering in the render_ast function. Specifically, we need  │
│ to ensure that a 1-element tuple like (1,) is rendered as (1,)     │
│ instead of (1).                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                            ✅ Reasoning                            │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue arises from a conditional check in the render_ast        │
│ function that removes the trailing comma when the tuple has only   │
│ one element. This is incorrect because a 1-element tuple should    │
│ retain the trailing comma for clarity and correctness.             │
│                                                                    │
│ We will modify the condition that determines whether to remove the │
│ trailing comma, ensuring it is only removed when the tuple has     │
│ more than one element.                                             │
