│ ┃          Patch to fix 1-element tuple rendering issue          ┃ │
│ ┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛ │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  [file]sphinx/ext/autodoc.py[/file]                                │
│  [original]                                                        │
│  def render_ast(node):                                             │
│      if isinstance(node, tuple):                                   │
│          # Original code that renders tuples without considering   │
│  trailing commas                                                   │
│          return f"({', '.join([render_ast(child) for child in      │
│  node])})"                                                         │
│  [/original]                                                       │
│  [patched]                                                         │
│  def render_ast(node):                                             │
│      if isinstance(node, tuple):                                   │
│          # Check if the tuple has only one element                 │
│          if len(node) == 1:                                        │
│              # Add trailing comma when tuple has only one element  │
│              return f"({', '.join([render_ast(child) for child in  │
│  node])},)"                                                        │
│          else:                                                     │
│              # Render tuples with normal formatting                │
│              return f"({', '.join([render_ast(child) for child in  │
│  node])})"                                                         │
│  [/patched]                                                        │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ The patch addresses the issue by adding a check for single-element │
│ tuples. When a tuple has only one element, the trailing comma is   │
│ added to preserve the correct formatting. This change ensures that │
│ both single-element tuples and multi-element tuples are rendered   │
│ correctly.                                                         │
